    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n7253" root="حجو" body-key="H">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">حَجٍ</span></b> : see <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">حَجِىٌّ</span>. ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">إِنَّهُ لَحَجِىٌ إِلَى بَنِى فُلَانٍ</span>
means <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">لَا جِئٌ لَهُمْ</span> [i. e. <i>Verily he is betaking himself for refuge,</i> or <i>protection, to the sons of such
a one;</i> like <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">لَحَجِئٌ</span>: but by rule it should be
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">لَحَجٍ</span>; and thus, perhaps, it is correctly written].
(AZ, TA.)

